  "id": "muller-lyer-illusion",
  "term": "Müller-Lyer illusion",
  "definition": "The Müller-Lyer illusion is a classic geometric illusion in which a line appears to have a different length depending on whether its ends are marked like arrow tails or arrowheads. In other words, the perceived length changes even though the physical line itself does not.",
